                "text": "Analyse the training examples:\nIn each example, a 10x10 grid with background color 5 contains several pixels of color 0.\nNotice that the pixels of color 0 appear only in certain columns!\nSpecifically:\nIn Example 1:\n0s appear at columns:\n- col 1: replaced by 1\n- col 3: replaced by 2\n- col 5: replaced by 3\n- col 8: replaced by 4\nWait, there are exactly 4 distinct columns with 0s!\nColumns with 0 in Ex 1: [1, 3, 5, 8]\nSorted order of columns:\n1st column from left: col 1 -> color 1\n2nd column from left: col 3 -> color 2\n3rd column from left: col 5 -> color 3\n4th column from left: col 8 -> color 4\n\nLet's check Example 2:\nColumns with 0:\ncol 0 (row 2, 6, 9)\ncol 5 (row 0, 4, 6)\ncol 6 (row 0, 2, 5, 6, 8)\ncol 9 (row 1, 4, 6)\nSorted columns: [0, 5, 6, 9]\ncol 0 -> color 1\ncol 5 -> color 2\ncol 6 -> color 3\ncol 9 -> color 4\nAll 0s in col 0 become 1.\nAll 0s in col 5 become 2.\nAll 0s in col 6 become 3.\nAll 0s in col 9 become 4.\n\nLet's check Example 3:\nColumns with 0:\ncol 2 (row 5)\ncol 3 (row 1, 3, 7)\ncol 4 (row 1, 2, 6, 9)\ncol 7 (row 0, 2, 5, 7, 9)\nSorted columns: [2, 3, 4, 7]\ncol 2 -> color 1\ncol 3 -> color 2\ncol 4 -> color 3\ncol 7 -> color 4\n\nEverything matches perfectly!\nRule:\nFind all distinct columns that contain at least one 0.\nSort these columns in ascending order of column index.\nReplace the 0s in the 1st column with 1, 2nd with 2, 3rd with 3, 4th with 4 (and so on, 1, 2, 3, 4...).\nAll 5s remain unchanged.\n\nI am ready for the test input. Please provide the test input grid.",
